{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-74080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{ }0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=2 \\\\ 0=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74080" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02121a74c9b9911bc467d99fe587801339acbe4a36dda4635c172043838d67a7"} {"question" "q-74080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-15"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74080" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix given by $L=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k-11 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(L).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(L),$ then the equation $Lx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[L\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[L\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & k-11 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -10 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k-11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k-11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ 0=k-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-16,$ which means that $k=16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74212" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02121a74c9b9911bc467d99fe587801339acbe4a36dda4635c172043838d67a7"} {"question" "q-74212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-16"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74212" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "16"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2}+{x}_{3}{m}_{3},$ and ${m}_{1}$, ${m}_{2}$, and ${m}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=10 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2}+2(-1) & =10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}-2 & =10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} & =12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+(-4)-5(-1) & =2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+1 & =2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${m}_{1},$ ${m}_{2},$ and ${m}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{1}}+(-4)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{2}}+(-1)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4)\\cdot (-1)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02121a74c9b9911bc467d99fe587801339acbe4a36dda4635c172043838d67a7"} {"question" "q-74223" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74223" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-74223" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-110974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-110974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k-2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 0=k-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-10,$ which means that $k=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-110974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "02121a74c9b9911bc467d99fe587801339acbe4a36dda4635c172043838d67a7"} {"question" "q-110974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-110974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-15"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-110974" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-111050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073392/state.json" "file_sha256" "cd209de1bfe2f60d9ed1f76ddce4badcbbb7e03775c0cd288b1775aa5087c129"} {"question" "q-111050" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{4}=-2 \\\\ 0=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=2.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" 